    "pr-1270": {
      "expected": {"file_count": 6, "hunk_count": 11, "body_count": 1, "issue_comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "review_comment_count": 0},
      "body_segments": [
        {"line_index": 0, "line_text": "Proof-of-concept decoupling render and update loops", "kind": "requirement", "disposition_rows": ["R1270-01"]},
        {"line_index": 2, "line_text": "Uses timers to trigger events rather than a loop - should allow (pretty much) arbitrary intervals between render and update steps.", "kind": "requirement", "disposition_rows": ["R1270-01", "R1270-09"]},
        {"line_index": 4, "line_text": "TODO before we can even *consider* merging this:", "kind": "context_no_requirement", "disposition_rows": []},
        {"line_index": 5, "line_text": " - Drag the GameState update out of the \"owning\" UI element", "kind": "requirement", "disposition_rows": ["R1270-02"]},
        {"line_index": 6, "line_text": " - Fixup the hardcoded timings for each time", "kind": "requirement", "disposition_rows": ["R1270-09"]},
        {"line_index": 7, "line_text": " - Find a decent way of aligning frame rate to running screens?", "kind": "requirement", "disposition_rows": ["R1270-03"]},
        {"line_index": 8, "line_text": " - Should UI update and render be a single event anyway?", "kind": "requirement", "disposition_rows": ["R1270-03"]},
        {"line_index": 9, "line_text": " - Use existing TICKS_PER_SECOND etc. constants rather than hardcoded test values", "kind": "requirement", "disposition_rows": ["R1270-09"]},
        {"line_index": 10, "line_text": " - Are SDL timers accurate enough? The documentation doesn't really guarantee much, but is this fine for a game?", "kind": "requirement", "disposition_rows": ["R1270-12"]},
        {"line_index": 11, "line_text": " - locked_queue is a quick dirty untested wrapper around std::queue to add a mutex, doesn't instantly crash at least...", "kind": "requirement", "disposition_rows": ["R1270-04"]},
        {"line_index": 12, "line_text": " - What happens on exit? Race conditions with locked_queue?", "kind": "requirement", "disposition_rows": ["R1270-04", "R1270-06"]},
        {"line_index": 13, "line_text": " - What happens if we can't keep up? I think the locked_queue will just drop events over it's arbitrary limit if non blocking. Would this happen to starve one event?", "kind": "requirement", "disposition_rows": ["R1270-05", "R1270-07"]},
        {"line_index": 14, "line_text": " - Everything running in a single thread could cause issues, especially if ahead in the render queue so the swap blocks", "kind": "requirement", "disposition_rows": ["R1270-07", "R1270-08"]}
      ],
